# Trivy CVE allowlist for @usetheo/memory standalone image.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-ID|REASON|SUNSET-DATE
#
# Sunset discipline:
#   - CRITICAL CVEs: sunset ≤ 30 days
#   - HIGH CVEs:     sunset ≤ 60 days
#   - MEDIUM CVEs:   sunset ≤ 90 days
#
# Lines beginning with `#` are comments (Trivy treats them as ignored).
# Each non-comment line must be a bare CVE ID (the pipe-delimited fields
# above are stripped before Trivy reads the file — see scripts hook in
# the docker-publish workflow if/when the allowlist needs entries).
#
# At v0.1.0-alpha this file is intentionally EMPTY — no production CVE
# has been allowlisted yet. New entries require a sunset date written
# next to the CVE ID on the SAME line via a `# sunset: YYYY-MM-DD` trailing
# comment for human review.
#

# ── OpenSSL / libssl3 in the distroless runtime base (added 2026-06-30, issue #86) ──
# Runtime = gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot @sha256:13593b75… which still
# ships libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2. The fixes (3.0.19 / 3.0.20-1~deb12u2) are PUBLISHED in
# Debian but NOT yet in the distroless rebuild. We cannot `apt upgrade` a distroless
# runtime (no shell/apt), and switching to node:22-slim to patch would ENLARGE the attack
# surface (shell + apt + more packages) — a worse trade for a Node/amd64 server. The
# CRITICAL (CVE-2026-31789) is a 32-bit-only heap overflow → NOT exploitable on this amd64
# image; the HIGH ones are DANE-TLSA / CMS / PKCS7 paths node TLS does not exercise.
# ACTION: re-evaluate at sunset OR when distroless ships libssl3 ≥ 3.0.20-1~deb12u2
# (track: re-run docker-publish; if the base updated, delete these lines).
# sunset: 2026-07-30  (CRITICAL ≤ 30d per deps-audit-golden-rule; the whole set re-checked together)
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390
CVE-2026-45447
